1c:["$","p",null,{"children":"在多个文本位置并行采样 reasoning，以可学习的开始和结束标记界定思考。mixture head 组合原预测与思考后的预测，再用真实后续文本的预测改善作为 REINFORCE 信号，同时更新标记及 model weights。"}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]
1e:["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"沿用原文的一般文本训练设置作演示：给定关于某人忘带雨伞的前缀，Model 在该位置采样短 Rationale，再预测后续文本。比较有无思考的预测质量，好的思考得到较高训练信号。实际训练会在多个位置并行处理，并用 Mixing Head 混合预测。这个天气句子是教学构造，不是论文报告的样本。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]
1f:["$","section","mathematics",{"id":"mathematics","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"06"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Mathematical Foundations"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"从符号、直觉与简单例子理解理论。"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"核心信号是 Thought 对未来文本 Log-Likelihood 的帮助。离散 Rationale 无法像连续向量那样直接求导，因此使用 REINFORCE 风格估计：高于基线的奖励提高该 Rationale 的生成概率。Mixing Head 学习在有无 Thought 的 Logits 之间插值，避免初期低质量 Thought 破坏原能力。下面是简化估计，不包含原文所有并行与非短视细节。"}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"math-block","aria-label":"数学表达式","children":"R(r) ≈ log p(future | prefix,r)\n∇J ≈ (R(r)−baseline) · ∇log p(r|prefix)\nMixed logits = α·logits_thought + (1−α)·logits_base"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"把 Rationale 当作一个会被采样的动作 r，就能理解 Policy Gradient。它如果让真实后续文本更容易预测，R(r) 会较高；减去 Baseline 后得到相对好坏的信号。乘上 ∇log p(r|prefix)，正信号会提高这类 Thought 的采样倾向，负信号则降低它。Logit 是 Softmax 前的分数，Mixing Head 学习的 α 控制 Thought 路径与普通路径的混合。这里列的是教学近似；论文使用跨后续位置的学习信号，不能将单个 Token 概率提升当作已经学会一般推理的证据。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
20:["$","section","experiments",{"id":"experiments","children":[[["$","span","results",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"results"}],["$","span","observation",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"observation"}]],["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"07"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Experiments & Claims"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"Research Question → Experiment → Answer"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-paper","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-paper","children":"Paper Claim"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Question：普通文本中的潜在思考训练能否改善预测并迁移到推理？→ Experiment：训练含 Thought 的 Model，检查语言建模及推理任务，分析 Thought 长度和相关组件。→ Answer：作者报告收益，但产生的文字是否忠实反映内部计算，需要另外的干预证据。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-paper","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-paper","children":"Paper Claim"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"摘要报告，继续 pre-training 后 GSM8K zero-shot 成绩从 5.9% 升至 10.9%，CommonsenseQA 从 36.3% 升至 47.2%，且困难词元的预测改善。这些任务没有单独 fine-tuning，但结果仍限于所研究的 model、语料和训练规模。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
21:["$","section","takeaways",{"id":"takeaways","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"08"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Takeaways"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"这篇论文改变了哪些判断？"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Quiet-STaR 的监督来自未来文本，优化目标首先是预测质量。Thought 更像一个待学习的中间计算通道，流畅或长并不代表更有用。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
22:["$","section","assumptions",{"id":"assumptions","children":[[["$","span","limits",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"limits"}]],["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"09"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Most Fragile Assumption"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"哪一个假设失效会动摇方法？"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"最脆弱的假设是更好预测文本意味着学到可迁移 Reasoning。文体模式、常见叙事和局部词汇线索也能提高 Likelihood，却未必帮助需要新计算的任务。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-inference","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-inference","children":"Inference"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"预测后文更好不等于中间解释在逻辑上真实，model 仍以外部文本提供的信号学习。并行采样与额外 reasoning 增加计算需求；实验不表明系统能创造新训练算法，也不证明持续扩大 reasoning 长度会获得无界改进。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","paper",{"href":"#reference-paper","aria-label":"来源 1: Quiet-STaR: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Think Before Speaking · v2","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
23:["$","section","reproduction",{"id":"reproduction","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"10"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"One-Week Reproduction"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"用一周检验一个最小且明确的命题。"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-hypothesis","children":"Hypothesis"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Day 1–2：建立小型可执行算术文本，限制 Thought 长度。Day 3–5：比较普通训练、随机 Thought 与奖励加权 Thought。Day 6–7：测未见运算组合，并将 Thought 替换或打乱，判断收益是否依赖其内容。"}],"$undefined",null]}]]]}]]}]
24:["$","section","counterexample",{"id":"counterexample","children":["$undefined",["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"11"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Counterexample Design"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"如何构造有辨识力的反例？"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-hypothesis","children":"Hypothesis"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"训练文本中固定用某种措辞对应答案，测试时打乱措辞与运算关系。如果 Thought 只重复文体线索，训练 Likelihood 提高但结构迁移失败，就能拆开预测捷径与推理能力。"}],"$undefined",null]}]]]}]]}]
25:["$","section","follow-up",{"id":"follow-up","children":[[["$","span","outlook",{"className":"anchor-alias","id":"outlook"}]],["$","span",null,{"className":"reading-section-number","children":"12"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Follow-up Research"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-question","children":"从缺陷与需求推导新的研究问题。"}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"analysis-block analysis-hypothesis","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"claim-label claim-hypothesis","children":"Hypothesis"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"研究潜在 Thought 的功能可识别性：对 Thought 进行语义保持改写与逻辑破坏干预，找出哪些内容真正决定后续计算。相对 STaR 的终点筛选，这要求因果验证中间过程。目标是建立可迁移计算的判据，而非增加思考 Token 数量。"}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"block-citations","children":[["$","a","2203.14465",{"href":"#reference-2203.14465","aria-label":"来源 2: STaR: Bootstrapping Reasoning With Reasoning","children":["[",2,"]"]}]]}]]}]]]}]]}]
